[h1]Advanced Targeting Hotkeys[/h1]

Filtered target acquisition for X4: Foundations, built on the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2181]Native Hotkey API[/url]: every action is bindable in the game's own keybinding UI.

[h2][b]Overview[/b][/h2]

Vanilla [b]Next Target[/b] / [b]Previous Target[/b] cycle through everything around you. This mod adds a [b]sticky filter[/b]: each acquisition hotkey targets the nearest matching object and remembers the category, so Next/Previous walk only enemies, stations, or the turrets of the ship you're attacking. Any other target change (a mouse click, a vanilla key, the target leaving the sector) drops the filter.

[b]Narrow Filter to Selected Type[/b] pins the filter to the exact type of the current target: one turret model on a destroyer, or one ship type in a mixed wing.

[h2]Auto-switch when target is lost[/h2]

For enemies, missiles, collectables and surface elements, a target that is destroyed, collected or no longer hostile (pilot bailed out) is replaced by the next one in the list:
[list]
[*] Surface elements prefer one in line of sight (can be switched off).
[*] When the last element of a kind is gone, you get the hull itself.
[*] With nothing left, the target is left alone, silently.
[/list]
Other categories drop the filter when the target dies, unless [b]Keep the filter when the target is destroyed[/b] is on.

