[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Hotkeys[/b][/h2]

All 20 actions work while piloting a ship with no menu open. None are bound by default: assign them under [b]Options > Hotkey Management > Hotkey Bindings[/b].

[h2]Acquisition[/h2]

Each targets the nearest match and sets the filter to its category:
[list]
[*] [b]Target Nearest Enemy[/b], [b](XS-M)[/b], [b](L-XL)[/b] - hostile ships, drones, mines, missiles and explosives, or ships of that size class.
[*] [b]Target Nearest Incoming Missile[/b] - a missile aimed at you.
[*] [b]Target Nearest Own Ship[/b], [b]for Landing[/b] - not the one you fly; the second only those with a bay that fits your ship.
[*] [b]Target Nearest Station[/b], [b]Gate[/b] (also accelerators and highway entries), [b]Collectable[/b] (dropped wares, lockboxes), [b]Asteroid[/b].
[*] [b]Target Surface Element[/b], [b]Engine[/b], [b]Turret[/b], [b]Shield Generator on Selected Object[/b] - working elements of the selected ship or station only, or of the last hull you worked on. Docked ships are never included.
[*] [b]Target Active Mission Object[/b] - the gate or highway entrance on the route to your mission's objective.
[/list]
[h2]Navigation[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Select Next / Previous Target (Filtered)[/b] - walk the active filter by distance, wrapping around.
[*] [b]Deselect Target and Reset Filter[/b] - clears both.
[*] [b]Target Along Line of Sight[/b] - a cone from dead ahead, widening from 1 to 25 degrees; the first hit wins. Range follows the radar; capital ships, stations and gates are pickable further out.
[*] [b]Narrow Filter to Selected Type[/b] - needs a target from this mod's hotkeys, or any target with [b]Narrow the filter on any target[/b] on.
[/list]
[h2]When nothing matches[/h2]

A hotkey never substitutes another kind of object: the target stays, with a fail sound and a message naming the empty category. The one exception: a surface filter with nothing left on a hull gives you the hull.

[h2][b]Relationship to the vanilla targeting hotkeys[/b][/h2]

The vanilla [b]Target Management[/b] controls ignore the filter. Bind this mod's versions and clear [b]Target Closest Hostile[/b], [b]Target Object[/b], [b]Next / Previous Target[/b] and [b]Deselect Target[/b]. [b]Toggle Target Lock[/b] and [b]Next / Previous Surface Element[/b] stay useful.

[h2][b]Settings[/b][/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-AdvancedTargetingHotkeys/refs/heads/main/docs/images/hotkey_api.png[/img]

Under [b]Options > Hotkey Management > Advanced Targeting Hotkeys[/b]:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-AdvancedTargetingHotkeys/refs/heads/main/docs/images/settings.png[/img]
[list]
[*] [b]Hotkey Groups[/b] (all on) - a group turned off is never registered, which frees its Native Hotkey API slots after the next reload.
[*] [b]Keep the filter after acquiring a target[/b] (on) - off makes Next/Previous cycle everything, as in vanilla.
[*] [b]Extended range multiplier[/b] ([b]2[/b]) - how far beyond radar range large objects stay pickable.
[*] [b]Own ships checked for a free dock[/b] ([b]12[/b]) - caps the scan behind [i]for Landing[/i].
[*] [b]Prefer visible surface elements when a target is lost[/b] (on).
[*] [b]Narrow the filter on any target, not only a filtered one[/b] (off) - also allows a line-of-sight or mouse pick.
[*] [b]Keep the filter when the target is destroyed[/b] (off) - for categories without auto-switch.
[*] [b]Feedback[/b] (all on) - a sound, and messages when nothing is found or the filter is narrowed.
[/list]
Settings are stored per profile, like key bindings.

[h2]Debug logging[/h2]

Follows the [i]Native Hotkey API[/i]'s [b]Debug Logging[/b] setting. Lines are prefixed [b]AdvancedTargetingHotkeys:[/b]; start the game with [b]-debug general -logfile debuglog.txt[/b] to capture them.

[h2][b]Limitations[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Pilot mode only.
[*] Candidate lists are rebuilt on every key press; on a station with hundreds of surface elements that is measurable work.
[*] Uses up to 20 of the [i]Native Hotkey API[/i]'s 48 shared slots.
[/list]
